<title>ROMANIA: Bucharest first-tier stocks keep turnover high.</title>
<headline>Bucharest first-tier stocks keep turnover high.</headline>
<text>
<p>1350 GMT - Heavy first-tier trading on the Bucharest bourse on Wednesday kept turnover high, at 2.02 billion lei, close to the previous day's level.</p>
<p>* The two stocks listed on the first tier -- Azomures SA fertiliser maker and Oltchim SA chemical plant -- took more than 95 percent of turnover.</p>
<p>* But Azomures closed lower under selling pressure, shedding 20 lei to a 1,610 close.</p>
<p>* Oltchim closed 20 lei stronger at 1,650.</p>
<p>* Most share prices rose due to low supply.</p>
<p>* Traders said newcomer  AMEP SA, a food packaging company, had done well on its first day, trading 17,190 shares on turnover of 20.4 million lei.</p>
